Falsifies `socket_contract::ephemeral::verification::a_position_is_a_port_in_range_and_the_clock_never_runs_backwards`.

The defect: `port_at` takes the remainder modulo one more than the range, so the top position maps
past `HI`.

Expected to fail: the harness's range assertion on the port.

diff --git a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/socket_contract/src/lib.rs
@@ -432,7 +432,7 @@
     }
 
     fn port_at(position: u64) -> u16 {
-        LO + (position % SPAN) as u16
+        LO + (position % (SPAN + 1)) as u16
     }
 
